From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: mediatek: mt6897: support drive-strength

The MT6897 pins have a 3-bit drive field that goes from 2 mA to 16 mA in
2 mA steps, and the binding accepts drive-strength. Without a drive_set
callback the pinconf core returns -ENOTSUPP for it, so a pin group that
sets it fails to apply and its device does not probe. Use the rev1 helpers,
as MT8188 and MT8195 do.

The MediaTek driver writes the raw field instead (FLAG_DRIVE_SET_RAW in
pinctrl-mt6897.c in the OnePlus MT6897 kernel), so drive-strength = <2> in
a vendor device tree is 6 mA here.

---
 drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt6897.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt6897.c b/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt6897.c
index 5770d77..a5c567b 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt6897.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt6897.c
@@ -1710,6 +1710,8 @@ static const struct mtk_pin_soc mt6897_data = {
 	.bias_set_combo = mtk_pinconf_bias_set_combo,
 	.bias_get_combo = mtk_pinconf_bias_get_combo,
 	.pull_type = mt6897_pull_type,
+	.drive_set = mtk_pinconf_drive_set_rev1,
+	.drive_get = mtk_pinconf_drive_get_rev1,
 	.adv_drive_get = mtk_pinconf_adv_drive_get,
 	.adv_drive_set = mtk_pinconf_adv_drive_set,
 };
